To terminate a C program, you can use the exit() function from the stdlib.h library. This will cause your program to immediately stop executing and return control back to the operating system.

Here's an example of how to use the exit() function in a C program:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main()
{
    printf("Hello World!\n");

    // Terminate the program with status code 0 (success)
    exit(0);
}
```

In this example, the program prints "Hello World!" to the console and then calls the exit() function with a status code
